From 708305cf1c9b0e470325cba9f4717a61d4441b4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 04:09:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 86/97] sched: keep the running request's Mamba prefix
 checkpoint referenced until it finishes

In Mamba align mode a state block leaves the block table once the request has computed one block past it. When
that block is hashed it is the request's prefix checkpoint, and releasing it let a long concurrent session evict
it, so the next turn re-prefilled the whole conversation. The manager now keeps the newest hashed checkpoint
referenced until the request finishes, and admission reserves that block. VLLM_E2_MAMBA_RETAIN_CHECKPOINT
(default 1) switches it off. Scheduler tests cover eviction, admission, preemption and freeing.
